Conditionals in ansible 

Ansible can use conditionals to execute tasks or plays when certain conditions are met.

to use conditional use the when statement



ansible -m setup -a "filter=ansible_os_family" dev

---
- hosts: dev
  become: true
  become_user: root
  tasks:
          - name: Shutdown Debian Systems
            command: /sbin/shutdown -t now
            when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"

---
- hosts: dev
  tasks:
    - name: Ansible Loop
      debug:
        msg: "{{ item }}"
      loop:
        - "hello1"
        - "hello2"
        - "hello3"
        - "hello4"
      when: 
        (ansible_os_family == "Debian" and ansible_distribution_major_version|int >= 6) 
        and (item in ["hello1", "hello2"])

